<BaseLayout title="Accessories" description="Accessory drive spacing for BK1 and BK2, plus links to A/C, gas pedal, clutch, alternator, and power steering guides for LS Gen Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Accessories</h1>
  <p>Accessory drive spacing, A/C retention, pedal choice, and clutch hydraulics all affect how "daily-able" the finished car feels.</p>

  <h2>Accessory Drive Spacing</h2>
  <p>
    On a BK1, get a Corvette-spacing front accessory drive. F-body (middle) spacing can work, but you want as much room as possible between the engine and the radiator fans.
    The BK2 has about 1.5" more front clearance. See <a href="/guides/cooling#clearance">Cooling</a> for measurements.
  </p>

